---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import FeatureRow from '../../components/FeatureRow.astro';
import IdleCounter from '../../components/IdleCounter.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What are telehealth credentialing services?', a: 'Telehealth credentialing services enroll clinicians with payers so they can bill in-network. Anvil does 50-state credentialing: roster-add under existing contracts for turnaround in weeks, then full enrollment under your own PC.' },
  { q: 'What is credentialing turnaround time on Anvil?', a: 'Roster-adds under existing contracts typically take weeks. Full enrollment under a new entity is commonly 90 to 120 days per payer when unmanaged; we track every file to the day so the parts you control do not sit.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between a roster-add and full enrollment?', a: 'A roster-add attaches a clinician to a group contract that already exists. It is paperwork plus payer processing, usually weeks. Full enrollment credentials the clinician and links them to a contract in your own entity\'s name, which is where the 90 to 120 days per payer comes from. Anvil does the first for speed and the second for ownership.' },
  { q: 'Do our clinicians need to be credentialed twice?', a: 'Primary source verification is done once and reused. The payer-facing enrollment happens under our PC first and under yours later. Most of the second pass is automated from the first.' },
  { q: 'Which applications are automated?', a: 'Fillable PDF applications and the major national payer portals are largely automated through Homefront. The remaining work is follow-up and exceptions, which we track per application.' },
  { q: 'Can you handle Medicaid managed care panels?', a: 'Yes. Medicaid MCO enrollment is state-specific and often the slowest. We work Medicaid MCO panels state by state, closed-panel exception paths included.' },
  { q: 'How do I see status?', a: 'An enrollment tracker per clinician, per payer, per entity, with the next action and who owns it. Weekly summary to your ops lead.' },
];
---
<SubpageLayout
  metaTitle="Telehealth credentialing in weeks, tracked to the day"
  title="Credentialing that is measured in weeks, and tracked to the day."
  description="Telehealth credentialing services in weeks: 50-state credentialing, roster-add vs full credentialing, turnaround tracked to the day."
  eyebrow="Platform / Credentialing"
  sub="Telehealth credentialing services take weeks when someone is watching them, not the 90 to 120 days of an untracked file. We roster-add your clinicians under existing 50-state contracts first, then build full credentialing under your own PC while they bill."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Platform', path: '/platform' }, { name: 'Credentialing', path: '/platform/credentialing' }]}
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaTitle="Stop paying clinicians to wait."
  ctaBody="Send us your roster. We will tell you which payers are a roster-add and which are a full enrollment, and how long each takes."
  ctaPrimary={{ label: 'Get started', href: '/contact' }}
  ctaSecondary={{ label: 'See pricing', href: '/pricing' }}
>
  <Section>
    <FeatureRow eyebrow="Two passes, one file" title="Roster-add now. Full enrollment under your entity in parallel." bullets={[
      'Primary source verification done once, reused for both entities',
      'Roster-adds to our contracts submitted in week one',
      'Applications under your PC filed as soon as it is formed',
      'Automated fillable-PDF and portal applications through Homefront',
      'Tracker per clinician, per payer, per entity, with next action and owner',
    ]}>
      <p>Most of the calendar in credentialing is waiting and forgetting. We take the forgetting out and shrink the waiting by starting under contracts that already exist.</p>
    </FeatureRow>
  </Section>
  <Section tight>
    <IdleCounter />
  </Section>
</SubpageLayout>
